{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoDTSpectrumSplit","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoDTSpectrumSplit","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Init.Data.Int.Basic","lean:module:Init.Omega"],"declarations":25,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoDTSpectrumSplit.symmetric_scalar_blind_to_chirality","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoDTSpectrumSplit.symmetric_scalar_blind_to_chirality","kind":"theorem","line":247,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/FiveTwoDTSpectrumSplit.lean#L247-L258","doc":"**Scalar-shadow corollary** (bar-graded form of\n`no_scalar_matches_chirality_split_datum`). Any `τ`-symmetric integer reading `g`\n(`g a b = g b a`) assigns the *same* value to the chirality-swapped pair, so it\ncannot recover the ordered `5₂` datum, whose bar-odd part is nonzero (`= 1`).\n\"No scalar serves the datum\" ⇔ \"the bar-odd part is nonzero\". ","formalizes":[{"@id":"block:prop:fivetwo-dt-spectrum-split","label":"prop:fivetwo-dt-spectrum-split","md":"quantum-observable-universe/appendix-qvalues/fivetwo-dt-spectrum-split.md"}],"signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoDTSpectrumSplit.dtPair52_chiral","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoDTSpectrumSplit.dtPair52_chiral","kind":"theorem","line":243,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/FiveTwoDTSpectrumSplit.lean#L243-L245","doc":"**The `5₂` datum is genuinely chiral**: `τ` moves it (`(4,3) ↦ (3,4)`),\nbecause its bar-odd part is nonzero. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoDTSpectrumSplit.dtPair52_grading","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoDTSpectrumSplit.dtPair52_grading","kind":"theorem","line":239,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/FiveTwoDTSpectrumSplit.lean#L239-L241","doc":"Its bar-grading is `(even, odd) = (7, 1)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoDTSpectrumSplit.dtPair52","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoDTSpectrumSplit.dtPair52","kind":"def","line":236,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/FiveTwoDTSpectrumSplit.lean#L236-L237","doc":"The certified ordered `5₂` DT-constant pair `(4, 3)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoDTSpectrumSplit.barGrading_faithful","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoDTSpectrumSplit.barGrading_faithful","kind":"theorem","line":228,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/FiveTwoDTSpectrumSplit.lean#L228-L234","doc":"**Faithful reconstruction.** The ordered pair is recovered from its\nbar-grading (`2·dt⁺ = even + odd`, `2·dt⁻ = even − odd`): the `ℤ/2` grading loses\nno information, so the DT spectrum *is* its bar-graded datum. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoDTSpectrumSplit.barOddPair_negated","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoDTSpectrumSplit.barOddPair_negated","kind":"theorem","line":223,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/FiveTwoDTSpectrumSplit.lean#L223-L226","doc":"`τ` negates the bar-odd part (the `-1` eigenspace). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoDTSpectrumSplit.barEvenPair_fixed","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoDTSpectrumSplit.barEvenPair_fixed","kind":"theorem","line":218,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/FiveTwoDTSpectrumSplit.lean#L218-L221","doc":"`τ` fixes the bar-even part (the `+1` eigenspace). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoDTSpectrumSplit.barOddPair","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoDTSpectrumSplit.barOddPair","kind":"def","line":215,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/FiveTwoDTSpectrumSplit.lean#L215-L216","doc":"Bar-odd part of the pair (the `τ`-antisymmetric combination = `chiralityOdd`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoDTSpectrumSplit.barEvenPair","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoDTSpectrumSplit.barEvenPair","kind":"def","line":212,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/FiveTwoDTSpectrumSplit.lean#L212-L213","doc":"Bar-even part of the pair (the `τ`-symmetric combination). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoDTSpectrumSplit.barSwap_involutive","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoDTSpectrumSplit.barSwap_involutive","kind":"theorem","line":208,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/FiveTwoDTSpectrumSplit.lean#L208-L210","doc":"`τ` is an involution: `τ ∘ τ = id`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoDTSpectrumSplit.barSwap","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoDTSpectrumSplit.barSwap","kind":"def","line":203,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/FiveTwoDTSpectrumSplit.lean#L203-L206","doc":"The chirality involution `τ` on the ordered pair of `S⁺`/`S⁻` Stokes\nconstants (the mirror / `q ↦ q⁻¹` swap exchanging the two factorization\nconstants). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoDTSpectrumSplit.readings_all_distinct","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoDTSpectrumSplit.readings_all_distinct","kind":"theorem","line":180,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/FiveTwoDTSpectrumSplit.lean#L180-L188","doc":"**No single scalar serves all readings.** For chiral `5₂` the ι-even\nsum (`7`), the two spectrum members (`4`, `3`), and the ι-odd difference\n(`1`) are pairwise distinct — the amphichiral collapse of `4₁` (all equal\nto `3`) does not occur. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoDTSpectrumSplit.chirality_sum_seven","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoDTSpectrumSplit.chirality_sum_seven","kind":"theorem","line":177,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/FiveTwoDTSpectrumSplit.lean#L177-L178","doc":"The symmetric (ι-even) sum of the two chirality constants is `7`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoDTSpectrumSplit.chirality_odd_datum_ne_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoDTSpectrumSplit.chirality_odd_datum_ne_zero","kind":"theorem","line":164,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/FiveTwoDTSpectrumSplit.lean#L164-L167","doc":"The chirality datum is nonzero as an inequality (the honest \"genuine\ndatum\" form). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoDTSpectrumSplit.chirality_odd_datum_eq_one","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoDTSpectrumSplit.chirality_odd_datum_eq_one","kind":"theorem","line":156,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/FiveTwoDTSpectrumSplit.lean#L156-L162","doc":"**The 5₂ chirality datum is nonzero.** For the certified split\n`(S⁺ ↦ 4, S⁻ ↦ 3)` the ι-odd datum is `chiralityOdd 4 3 = 1 ≠ 0` — the\nbar-odd (ι-odd) channel receives a genuine, chirality-sourced Stokes\ndatum from `5₂`, which the amphichiral `4₁` (where it is `0`) cannot\nsupply. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoDTSpectrumSplit.chiralityOdd_antisym","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoDTSpectrumSplit.chiralityOdd_antisym","kind":"theorem","line":150,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/FiveTwoDTSpectrumSplit.lean#L150-L154","doc":"**The ι-odd datum is genuinely antisymmetric** under swapping the two\nchirality constants (the Stokes-constant analogue of `ω` being ι-odd). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoDTSpectrumSplit.chiralityOdd_degenerate","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoDTSpectrumSplit.chiralityOdd_degenerate","kind":"theorem","line":143,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/FiveTwoDTSpectrumSplit.lean#L143-L148","doc":"**On the amphichiral degeneracy the ι-odd datum vanishes.** When the\ntwo chirality constants coincide (the `4₁` case, one member), their\nantisymmetric datum is `0` — the Stokes-constant analogue of\n`omega_zero_on_iotaFixed`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoDTSpectrumSplit.chiralityOdd","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoDTSpectrumSplit.chiralityOdd","kind":"def","line":138,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/FiveTwoDTSpectrumSplit.lean#L138-L141","doc":"The ι-odd (antisymmetric) combination of the two chirality constants,\nover `Int` (core; the Stokes constants are integers — no archimedean\nstructure, §7c). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoDTSpectrumSplit.dt_spectrum_two_element","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoDTSpectrumSplit.dt_spectrum_two_element","kind":"theorem","line":123,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/FiveTwoDTSpectrumSplit.lean#L123-L127","doc":"**The 5₂ DT spectrum has two distinct members.** The constant carried\nby `S⁺` (`4`) differs from the constant carried by `S⁻` (`3`): unlike the\namphichiral `4₁`, a chiral knot's leading Stokes data is not served by a\nsingle integer. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoDTSpectrumSplit.fourone_carries_three","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoDTSpectrumSplit.fourone_carries_three","kind":"theorem","line":118,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/FiveTwoDTSpectrumSplit.lean#L118-L121","doc":"The `4₁` leading Stokes matrix carries the **single** off-diagonal\ninteger `3` (its `(0,1)` entry) — the amphichiral degeneracy where the\nspectrum collapses to one member. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoDTSpectrumSplit.sminus0_carries_three","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoDTSpectrumSplit.sminus0_carries_three","kind":"theorem","line":114,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/FiveTwoDTSpectrumSplit.lean#L114-L116","doc":"`S⁻(0)` carries the DT constant `3` (its `(0,2)` entry — the (97)\nfactorization constant). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoDTSpectrumSplit.splus0_carries_four","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoDTSpectrumSplit.splus0_carries_four","kind":"theorem","line":110,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/FiveTwoDTSpectrumSplit.lean#L110-L112","doc":"`S⁺(0)` carries the DT constant `4` (its `(0,1)` entry — the (96)\nfactorization constant). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoDTSpectrumSplit.Splus0_41","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoDTSpectrumSplit.Splus0_41","kind":"def","line":101,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/FiveTwoDTSpectrumSplit.lean#L101-L106","doc":"The `4₁` q→0 Stokes matrix `S⁺(0) = [[1,3],[0,1]]` (GGM eq 60,\n`StokesQZeroDTCount.Splus0`), carried as a `2×2` for the amphichiral\ncontrast. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoDTSpectrumSplit.Sminus0","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoDTSpectrumSplit.Sminus0","kind":"def","line":95,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/FiveTwoDTSpectrumSplit.lean#L95-L99","doc":"`S⁻(0)` for 5₂ — the glyph-decoded (97) factorization (constant `3`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoDTSpectrumSplit.Splus0","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoDTSpectrumSplit.Splus0","kind":"def","line":89,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/FiveTwoDTSpectrumSplit.lean#L89-L93","doc":"`S⁺(0)` for 5₂ — the glyph-decoded (96) factorization (constant `4`). ","signatureChunk":0}]}